},{"title":"police said","target":"https://wtop.com/charles-county/2026/05/guns-3d-printer-seized-from-2-students-after-firearms-found-at-charles-co-high-school/","line":106},{"title":"study","target":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S2468170926000032?via%3Dihub","line":112},{"title":"*awatford@stateline.org*","target":"mailto:awatford@stateline.org","line":116}],"metadata":{"title":"More states restrict 3D-printed firearms • Stateline","source":"https://stateline.org/2026/06/11/more-states-restrict-3d-printed-firearms/","author":["[[Amanda Watford]]"],"published":"2026-06-11","created":"2026-07-31","description":"For decades, making an untraceable firearm required specialized tools, technical expertise and hours of work. Today, it can start with a downloaded file and a consumer-grade 3D printer. As advances in additive manufacturing, commonly known as 3D printing, make it easier to produce firearms at home, lawmakers in a growing number of states are pursuing […]"},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[]},